    "body": "There seems to be two options here:\r\n  1. Check _contributes a script-blocking style sheet_ \"at the time response was fetched\"\r\n  2. Check _contributes a script-blocking style sheet_ \"the last time that the _linked resource fetch setup steps_ were run for _el_\"\r\n\r\nI don't think (2) is appropriate, because that algorithm could have run a second time for an entirely different resource by the time the process response steps end up running. Instead, what we want is to capture state from the last time those steps were run \"for _response_\" in particular, which I've tried to do in a hopefully-not-too-action-at-a-distance way here (see the thread's OP).",
